 ## Overview
-A compact storage format for 3x3 symmetric matrices, reducing the required memory from nine values to six by exploiting the property $M_{ij} = M_{ji}$. It serves as the foundational data structure for representing covariance matrices in Gaussian Splatting variants and stress tensors in scientific visualization, eliminating redundant storage and ensuring symmetry constraints are maintained by construction.
+The Symmetric Matrix Data Structure (SMat3) is a compact memory layout for representing 3x3 symmetric matrices by storing only the unique elements. It solves the problem of redundant storage in symmetric tensors, reducing memory footprint by 50% compared to a full 3x3 matrix. It sets itself apart from general matrix structures by enforcing symmetry constraints at the data level, ensuring $m_{ij} = m_{ji}$ without requiring runtime checks or explicit copying.
 
